{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987528-advice-on-a-homebrew-for-princess-the-hopeful","id":987528,"title":"Advice on a homebrew for Princess: The Hopeful","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-14T18:30:04-07:00","id":987528,"title":"Advice on a homebrew for Princess: The Hopeful","content":"I have an idea for a Cult Of Darkness to be used as antagonists for Princess: The Hopeful. My basic idea is a frat named Kama Thi. This frat is mostly seen as a group of college boys with a real hard-on for partying. But what no one knows is that the partying is really a veil they use to hide a sinister secret. I need advice on how I can make this work, what kind of stats to use and how big the cult should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T20:09:53-07:00","id":987572,"title":"","content":"Well, for starters, &quot;Kama&quot; and &quot;Thi&quot; aren't Greek letters, and you might want to take care to avoid using a real frat's letters unless you know what you're doing.<br /> <br /> I'd say that it should probably have two sides to it. The &quot;old blood&quot; members, the entrenched powerful people who run the show and keep the frat funded and run the fraternity on the macro-level (They decide the big rituals, choose who runs the chapters, help perform cleanup for botched shenanigans), and the actual student members that do the dirty work (and the pledges that get stuck doing the <i>really</i> dirty work, then got dumped if they're caught for the sake of plausible deniability).<br /> <br /> Using a fictitious frat as a cult is neat idea, considering they have sort of a cult-like image in pop culture, what with the weird initiation rituals and the really insular culture that leaves what goes on to outsiders' imaginations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T21:08:37-07:00","id":987591,"title":"","content":"First, why don't you ask the RPGnet thread? A lot of people don't know Princess exists over here.<br /> <br /> Second, methinks they should be a college frat first and a Dark Cult second-which is bad enough, as they embody the worst aspects of the rich and responsibility-less. David Cameron putting his dick in a pig comes to mind, as does the weird crap Skull and Bones gets up to.<br /> <br /> The real threat is that they Taint the children of the rich and powerful-who are usually rich and powerful themselves. This leads to entire generations of impulsive, power-hungry, and destructive leaders. I will refrain from making the obvious political joke here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T21:55:51-07:00","id":987603,"title":"","content":"Did you look at the Pleasure Principle? That cult is all about teaching people to be irresponsible hedonists and leading them into ever-deeper depths of depravity. I hadn't thought of them as a college fraternity, but that's just the sort of thing they <i>would</i> use as a cover if they happened to think of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:49:31-07:00","id":987867,"title":"","content":"I actually did not think of asking RPGnet. Also, i was thinking that the cult was governed by a council which is comprised of former members of the frat. I also had the idea that the frat was founded as a recruitment tool by a larger cult that was destroyed by the Princesses two years after the Moon Landing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}